{"title":"PLC/DCS Engineer Roadmap","role":"PLC/DCS Engineer","summary":"An Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering degree is strongly aligned with PLC/DCS engineering. The role combines industrial automation, process instrumentation, control systems, PLC programming, Distributed Control Systems (DCS), SCADA, industrial networking and plant operations.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 of UG","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"PLC/DCS Engineer is a realistic graduate-entry career. Common entry roles include Automation Engineer, PLC Engineer, Control & Instrumentation Engineer, Instrumentation Engineer, SCADA Engineer and Graduate Engineer Trainee."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"PLC/automation internships, instrumentation internships, SCADA projects and industrial training"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"PLC programming, DCS configuration, HMI/SCADA, process control and industrial networking"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"automation architecture, plant integration, functional safety and control-system leadership"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Industrial IoT, digital twins, edge computing, AI-based process optimisation and autonomous operations"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"PLC/DCS Engineers work across manufacturing, oil & gas, power generation, pharmaceuticals, chemicals, food processing, water treatment, automotive and other process industries."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 · Sem 1"},{"text":"C/Python, electrical 